    pr_ref:  # a27e
    description: "SPLIT OUT OF WI-pifaj per the G8 \"Reproducibility semantics\" scout (2026-07-21, g8_reproducibility_scout_findings_07212026.md). WI-pifaj's own residual is the docs-honesty spec fix (PR-A: correct the false \"byte-stable\" claim at spec:321, soften :72 / :1649). THIS item is the \"full byte-repro mode\" the scout recommended splitting into a separate work item.\n\nDESIGN DECISION — FLAG-GATED, uuid4 stays the DEFAULT. Chosen over an always-on structural de-overload to avoid churning the load-bearing `origin_run_id -> analysis_runs` FK, the asserted `uuid:` test contract, and every human run. aijo's survey layer would always pass `--reproducible`, so a flag fully serves it without touching the default / audit path. (An always-on structural split — segregate the uuid into its own audit field, make the deterministic id the FK unconditionally — stays available as a LATER hardening if the \"did you pass the flag?\" footgun bites; not needed to unblock aijo.)\n\nSCOPE under `--reproducible` (and/or honoring SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH):\n- Derive `execution_id` deterministically = hash(run_signature + repo_fingerprint + pass_id), TIMESTAMP-FREE. NOTE the spec's own documented sha256 recipe (spec:289 / ir.py) wrongly folds in `started_at` — drop it, or it still churns. Must stay unique-per-run-identity so the `origin_run_id -> analysis_runs` FK (validator F2, spec_validator.py:2091) still resolves. `origin_run_id` copies this id into every Symbol / Edge — the \"342/568 differing sorted-key lines\" amplifier (copy sites cli.py:9426/9444/9665; serialized ir.py:617 Symbol / :1014 Edge).\n- Omit / normalize wall-clock fields: `started_at` + `duration_ms` (ir.py:370 / :392) and top-level `generated_at` (schema.py:168).\n\nACCEPTANCE (folds the DET-4 guard): a property test asserting two `--reproducible` runs on identical input produce BYTE-IDENTICAL output, over the bakeoff corpus. This is the enforcement, not decoration — an unverified canonical-form claim is a silent-corruption risk.\n\nEFFORT: M (flag-gated) per the scout; L only if ever promoted to default + fixtures.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE — G8's other three items are distinct fingerprints on separate tracks: WI-fonod (grammar over-capture, bundle w/ WI-givad), INV-nogom (config_fingerprint runtime-flag blindness, demand-gated), WI-sijug (Symbol.fingerprint nulls, mostly policy-dissolved). The canonical-digest and survey-diff follow-ups are separate items; this one blocks the digest."  # a27e
    fields: {}  # a27e
